  {
    "id": "amended-09",
    "kind": "amended",
    "question": "If the computer running Foedrum dies, is the history of its batches lost?",
    "answer": "No, with one gap. The durable record lives in the Brewery repository on the `foedrum/state` branch (an append-only `events.jsonl` and the out docs per batch), committed and pushed at every step boundary, which in practice is the supervisor's next tick, at most one tick (5 s by default) later. Only events not yet pushed at that moment are lost with the machine; a new machine rebuilds SQLite, which is only the local index and working store, from the branch.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "path": "docs/adr/0011-state-in-the-brewery-repository.md",
        "lines": "9-11",
        "quote": "The **durable record** lives in the Brewery repository on a dedicated branch"
      },
      {
        "path": "docs/adr/0044-batch-leases-held-by-the-driver-and-one-command-log.md",
        "lines": "21-22",
        "quote": "[ADR 0024](0024-state-branch-layout-outbox-and-divergence.md) flushes the state branch at a step boundary."
      },
      {
        "path": "docs/adr/0002-event-sourced-engine-on-node-sqlite.md",
        "lines": "12",
        "quote": "Storage is **SQLite through the built-in `node:sqlite`** module"
      }
    ],
    "paraphrased": true,
    "stale": "ADR 0002: the event log, the single source of truth, is stored in a local SQLite file (so losing the machine loses the history, as ADR 0011's context notes).",
    "note": "ADR 0011 is itself amended (0024, 0044, 0263), but none of those moves the record off foedrum/state; 0263 line 12 confirms the decision stands.",
    "review": "hand"
  },
  {
