  {
    "id": "recipe-01",
    "kind": "recipe",
    "question": "Which lenses review a change in Nip, and at what effort?",
    "answer": "Four Tasters review the change side by side through the correctness, acceptance, security and design conformance lenses. Correctness, acceptance and security run at high effort; design conformance runs at the Taster's own effort.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "path": "defaults/recipes/nip.jsonc",
        "lines": "56-72",
        "quote": "\"id\": \"taste\","
      }
    ],
    "paraphrased": false,
    "note": "Header comment lines 10-11 state the Taster's own effort is medium; the step lines only omit effort for design-conformance.",
    "review": "model-triage"
  },
  {
    "id": "recipe-02",
    "kind": "recipe",
    "question": "If I only want a big job broken down into smaller pieces, does anything get coded, and who looks over the breakdown?",
    "answer": "Nothing is built in Mash: the Brewmaster reads the order and breaks it into sub-orders, and three Tasters review the plan side by side through the plan/coverage (on the planner model), plan/sizing and plan/naive-reader lenses; their findings send the plan back to the Brewmaster (two rounds per run, then the batch is Stuck with them open). The plan is then shown on the order's issue, where the batch waits Stuck until a person signs it off with foedrum approve.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "path": "defaults/recipes/mash.jsonc",
        "lines": "13",
        "quote": "Plan an order as sub-orders through three lenses, shown on its issue; nothing is built"
      },
      {
        "path": "defaults/recipes/mash.jsonc",
        "lines": "17-34",
        "quote": "{ \"id\": \"plan\", \"brewer\": \"brewmaster\" },"
      },
      {
        "path": "defaults/recipes/mash.jsonc",
        "lines": "1-8",
        "quote": "Mash, a plan of an order (ADR 0234): the Brewmaster reads the order and its repository and breaks"
      }
    ],
    "paraphrased": true,
    "review": "hand"
  },
  {
    "id": "recipe-03",
    "kind": "recipe",
    "question": "How does Decoction differ from Mash in how the plan is reviewed?",
    "answer": "Decoction runs Mash's steps but puts all seven plan lenses in the review group: coverage, sizing, naive-reader, order-and-overlap, testability, recipe-fit and security. Coverage and security run on the planner model.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "path": "defaults/recipes/decoction.jsonc",
        "lines": "1",
        "quote": "Mash's steps, with all seven plan lenses in"
      },
      {
        "path": "defaults/recipes/decoction.jsonc",
        "lines": "22-31",
        "quote": "\"lens\": \"plan/coverage\","
      }
    ],
    "paraphrased": false,
    "note": "Mash's three lenses are in recipe-02 (mash.jsonc 26-31).",
    "review": "model-triage"
  },
  {
    "id": "recipe-04",
    "kind": "recipe",
    "question": "When a new ticket comes in, how is it decided which workflow will handle it?",
    "answer": "By its `recipe:<name>` label: that label wins. Under foedrum serve an issue without one is not given a recipe by itself (it waits for the routing deadline, then is Stuck on routing). When a person runs foedrum mash on it, or foedrum brew on an unlabelled issue (which uses the Brewery's default recipe, mash-in unless defaultRecipe says otherwise), Mash-in runs: the Innkeeper reads the order and suggests one of the Brewery's recipes with its reason, the engineer's answer chooses the recipe, the batch starts it from its first step, and the issue is labelled with it.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "path": "docs/design/intake/routing.md",
        "lines": "3",
        "quote": "**Routing:** a `recipe:<name>` label wins, and `foedrum serve` chooses no recipe for an unlabelled issue by itself;"
      },
      {
        "path": "docs/design/intake/routing.md",
        "lines": "8",
        "quote": "`foedrum mash <issue>` routes a Brewery issue's Ordered or routing-Stuck batch"
      },
      {
        "path": "docs/design/intake/routing.md",
        "lines": "12",
        "quote": "`foedrum brew <n>` on an issue with no recipe label"
      },
      {
        "path": "defaults/recipes/mash-in.jsonc",
        "lines": "1-4",
        "quote": "Mash-in, the first step of a mash (ADR 0232): the Innkeeper reads the order and asks one question,"
      },
      {
        "path": "defaults/recipes/mash-in.jsonc",
        "lines": "10",
        "quote": "\"steps\": [{ \"id\": \"innkeep\", \"brewer\": \"innkeeper\", \"chooses\": \"recipe\" }]"
      },
      {
        "path": "defaults/brewers/innkeeper.md",
        "lines": "29",
        "quote": "Read the order in {order} and suggest which recipe of {recipes} brews it."
      }
    ],
    "paraphrased": true,
    "review": "hand"
  },
  {
    "id": "recipe-05",
    "kind": "recipe",
    "question": "In Deep-brew, what happens to mutants that Brett's mutation step finds the tests do not catch?",
    "answer": "Each surviving mutant is a finding that goes back to the Gauger, who adds tests that catch it; the red proof checks they fail and Cellarman writes the code again. This happens at most two rounds per run, then the batch is Stuck with the survivors open.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "path": "defaults/recipes/deep-brew.jsonc",
        "lines": "49-56",
        "quote": "Each mutant the tests let survive is a finding that goes back to the Gauger"
