      {
        "path": "defaults/recipes/nip.jsonc",
        "lines": "46-49",
        "quote": "A failure goes back to Cellarman, whichever step broke it; the Finer then runs again."
      }
    ],
    "paraphrased": true,
    "review": "model-triage"
  },
  {
    "id": "recipe-09",
    "kind": "recipe",
    "question": "Is there a rule of thumb for how large each piece of a planned job should be?",
    "answer": "The sizing lens checks that each sub-order is about 1,000 lines or one mechanism, so one batch can build it and a person can review it. That is a measure, not a limit: an entry a little past the mark that is plainly one mechanism is not reported.",
